@startuml rendering-pipeline-flowchart-bitmap-backbuffer
title Gondwana - BitmapBackbuffer / CPU Rendering
' This diagram expands the bitmap steps inside Engine.DoForegroundTasks.
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam activity {
  BackgroundColor #E5F3EB
  BorderColor #377858
  ArrowColor #377858
}

|Engine thread|
start
:Frame due at TargetFPS (or no throttle);
:BeforeFrameRender;
:Update surface effects;
:Update DirectDrawings;
:RenderSurfaceHost.RenderToBackbuffer(tick);
:BitmapBackbuffer.BeginFrame();
:RenderBackbufferBegin;

if (No views or visible scene layers?) then (yes)
  :Clear whole bitmap backbuffer;
  :Scene.FullRefreshNeeded = false;
else (no)
  if (Scene full refresh, or dirty full-view composition?) then (yes)
    :Enqueue visible world rectangles\nfor all views and layers;
  endif
  if (Scene.IsDirty?) then (yes)
    :For each View in Z order;
    :Collect dirty screen regions from layer RefreshQueues;
    :Clip to view, excluding blocking higher views;
    :Apply view presentation effects;
    :Draw visible layers back-to-front,\nscene tiles, sprites, and layer drawings;
    :Draw view overlays;
    :Invoke post-scene canvas hooks;
    :Clear consumed layer RefreshQueues;
    :Scene.FullRefreshNeeded = false;
  else (no)
    :RenderBackbufferNoOp;\n(no dirty-region drawing);
  endif
endif

:RenderBackbufferEnd;
:RenderSurfaceHost.PresentBackbufferToAdapter();
:BitmapBackbuffer.EndFrame();
if (Full presentation needed?) then (yes)
  :Snapshot and present full bitmap;
else (no)
  :Snapshot and present dirty rectangle\nwhen nonempty;
endif
:Clear backbuffer dirty rectangle;
:BitmapBackbuffer.BeginFrame()\n(prepare for next frame);
:AfterFrameRender;
:PostCycle timers;
stop

|Desktop UI thread|
start
:WinForms SKControl paints cached SKImage\nor Avalonia updates WriteableBitmap;
stop

note right
  No-op scene rendering exits RenderToBackbufferBitmap,
  NOT Engine.DoForegroundTasks: presentation and callbacks
  still proceed. Browser bitmap hosting is also supported.
end note
@enduml
